---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const {production=false}=Astro.props;
---
<Base title={production ? "About Tracy Osborn" : "About Tracy — page preview"} description="Designer, former startup founder, and general manager at TinySeed and MicroConf. Originally from Northern California, now in Toronto." editorial noindex={!production} navigationEmail={false} bodyClass="about-page" width="col-lg-10 col-lg-offset-1" navigation={[["/#work","Current work"],[production?"/about/":"/mockups/about/","About"],["/articles/","Writing archive"]]}>
  <Fragment slot="preview-bar">{!production && <div class="about-preview-bar">About page draft <a href="/">Back to the live site ↗</a></div>}</Fragment>
  <header slot="intro" class="about-opening">
    <div class="about-introduction">
      <h1>A little more<br/>about me.</h1>
      <p class="about-lead">I’m a designer, former startup founder, and the general manager at TinySeed and MicroConf.</p>
      <p>I grew up in Northern California, studied art and design at Cal Poly, and now live in Toronto. I’ve been making websites since I was twelve.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="about-portrait"><img src="/static/images/tracy-osborn_atom-images.jpg" alt="Tracy Osborn, photographed outdoors at DjangoCon US" width="1000" height="667"/><figcaption>DjangoCon US, 2017. Photo by Adam Gregory / AtomImages.</figcaption></figure>
  </header>
  <div class="about-story">
    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>Design came first.</h2>
      <p>I started college in computer science, then switched to art and design. I liked making websites, but the way programming was taught didn’t click for me. I wanted to build something I could actually use.</p>
      <p>A few years later, I had an idea for a business and needed to build it myself. That’s when Python and Django finally made sense. Learning by making a real project worked much better for me than starting with theory.</p>
      <p>That experience became <em>Hello Web App</em>, my books for people learning to build their first web app. I later wrote <em>Hello Web Design</em> for people coming at design from the other direction.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>Then I ran a company.</h2>
      <p>WeddingLovely started as a directory of wedding vendors and grew into a marketplace and planning app. I designed it, built it, joined 500 Startups, and spent eight years figuring out how to keep a small business going.</p>
      <p>I shut it down in 2018. I’ve written quite a bit about that decision, including how a business can be technically profitable and still take more from you than it gives back.</p>
      <a class="about-reading" href="/articles/why-i-shut-down-weddinglovely/">Why I shut down WeddingLovely <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </section>
    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>Finding my place at TinySeed.</h2>
      <p>After WeddingLovely, I wasn’t sure where I’d fit. Running a company had given me a broad set of skills, but I didn’t feel like an obvious match for any one job.</p>
      <p>I joined TinySeed as program manager in 2019. It turned out that being comfortable with design, development, and all the other parts of running a business was useful when building an accelerator from scratch.</p>
      <p>Today, I lead operations across TinySeed and MicroConf. My work has grown to include our events and founder programs, including helping launch the SaaS Institute.</p>
      <p>I’ve been on the other side of the table as a founder. I like being able to use that experience to help other people with their businesses.</p>
      <a class="about-reading" href="/#work">More about my current work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </section>
    <section class="about-section about-outdoors">
      <h2>There’s also a lot of hiking.</h2>
      <p>Outside of work, I like running, hiking, backpacking, camping, and rafting. In 2014, I solo-hiked the John Muir Trail in California.</p>
      <figure><img src="/static/home/whitney-retouched.jpg" alt="Mountain ridges and a lake beneath storm clouds near Mount Whitney" width="1578" height="996" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>From my John Muir Trail trip, 2014.</figcaption></figure>
      <p>One night near Mount Whitney involved thunderstorms and a very questionable campsite. I wrote about that, too.</p>
      <a class="about-reading" href="/articles/external-dangerous-thing/">The most dangerous thing I’ve ever done <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </section>
    {!production && <aside class="about-draft-notes">
      <details><summary>Draft notes &amp; sources</summary>
        <p>This preview uses the existing 2017 portrait. A newer photo would be a good next step. The outdoor interests come from the original About page; please confirm they still feel current.</p>
        <p>Sources: <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tracyosborn/">LinkedIn profile and public posts</a>, <a href="https://tinyseed.com/people">TinySeed’s team page</a>, <a href="https://nostarch.com/blog/womens-history-month-spotlight-deal-4">2021 No Starch Press interview</a>, and the original About page and articles in this archive. LinkedIn was available through public search excerpts, rather than a full profile read.</p>
      </details>
    </aside>}
  </div>
  <footer slot="footer" class="editorial-footer"><a href="/">Current work</a><a href="/articles/">Writing archive</a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tracyosborn/">LinkedIn</a></footer>
</Base>
<style is:global>
  .about-preview-bar {display:flex;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:24px;padding:10px 18px;color:#888d7e;font:400 12px/1.6 Lato,sans-serif;}
  .about-opening {display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;align-items:center;gap:55px;margin:78px auto 75px;max-width:900px;}
  .editorial-site .about-opening h1 {font-size:4.7rem;line-height:.95;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:0 0 30px;}
  .about-opening p {font-size:1.14rem;line-height:1.8;font-weight:300;}
  .about-opening .about-lead {font:400 1.3rem/1.6 Lora,Georgia,serif;color:#55594d;letter-spacing:-.015em;}
  .about-portrait {margin:0;}
  .about-portrait img {width:100%;height:390px;object-fit:cover;object-position:60% center;}
  .about-page figcaption {font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.6;color:#888d7e;margin-top:12px;}
  .about-story {max-width:740px;margin:auto;}
  .about-section {margin-bottom:64px;}
  .about-section::before {content:"";display:block;width:48px;height:3px;background:#c59b3d;margin-bottom:29px;}
  .editorial-site .about-section h2 {font-size:2.65rem;line-height:1.12;margin:0 0 22px;}
  .about-section p {font-size:1.2rem;line-height:1.78;font-weight:300;}
  .about-section em {font-family:Lora,Georgia,serif;font-size:.94em;}
  .about-reading {font-size:1rem;line-height:1.8;}
  .about-outdoors figure {margin:32px 0;}
  .about-outdoors img {display:block;width:100%;height:auto;}
  .about-draft-notes {color:#888d7e;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.75;}
  .about-draft-notes summary {cursor:pointer;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px;}
  .about-draft-notes p {font-size:.9rem;}
  @media(max-width:767px){
    .about-opening {grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:25px;margin:45px 0 50px;}
    .editorial-site .about-opening h1 {font-size:3.8rem;}
    .about-opening .about-lead {font-size:1.22rem;}
    .about-opening p,.about-section p {font-size:1.14rem;line-height:1.75;}
    .about-portrait {max-width:500px;}
    .about-portrait img {height:auto;aspect-ratio:4/3;object-position:center;}
    .about-section {margin-bottom:48px;}
    .about-section::before {width:42px;margin-bottom:24px;}
    .editorial-site .about-section h2 {font-size:2.35rem;}
  }
</style>
